			"Message": "fix(Project): Align SCM provider handles between Mountain and Cocoon\n\nSubmodule synchronization addressing two critical issues:\n\n1. SCM Provider Handle Alignment (Common + Mountain + Cocoon):\n   - Common adds optional Handle field to SourceControlCreateDTO enabling Cocoon to supply its sequential allocator handle\n   - Mountain now honors caller-supplied Handle in CreateSourceControl rather than allocating via DJB hash\n   - Previously, group updates from Cocoon used sequential handles while Mountain keyed marker maps with DJB hash, causing \"Received group update for unknown provider handle\" warnings and empty SCM viewlet\n\n2. Recently-Opened Workspace Fallback (Mountain):\n   - Fixes boot seeding to probe RecentlyOpened.json (same source as webview's BuildInitialUrl) between env/CLI and CWD walk-up\n   - Resolves webview title showing \"Mountain\" while Cocoon payload shipped \"Land\"\n   - Fixes vscode.git scanning wrong root and SCM panel showing zeros despite untracked changes\n\n3. Dependency Updates:\n   - Mountain, Worker: Bump pozil/auto-assign-issue from 2.2.x to 3.0.0\n\nRefs: 3cfc021e (DTO serialization), 4c472e3 (event payload fixes)",
			"SHA": "072ef07cf9596928526c3330aedccd96136239b6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T14:48:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡟⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				10
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Synchronize submodules with Mountain event fixes and Sky webview bridge\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing critical fixes and a new feature:\n\n1. Mountain (ba479c6a) - Event Payload Alignment Fixes:\n   - Fix event channel names: terminal `opened`→`create`, `closed`→`exit`, debug `stop`→`sessionEnd`, statusbar `create`→`set-entry`, webview `message`→`post-message`, progress→`notification/progress-update`\n   - Correct payload keys to camelCase: OutputProvider, StatusBarProvider, TreeViewProvider, UserInterfaceProvider, Window\n   - Add parameter key fallback: probe camelCase first then snake_case for backward compatibility\n   - Fix SCM RootUri: reconstruct full URI from scheme/authority/path instead of emitting relative URLs\n   - Add command registry emissions for Sky's workbench command palette\n\n2. Sky (f0fabc61) - New Webview Post-Message Bridge:\n   - Add handler for `sky://webview/post-message` to dispatch `cel:webview:post-message` events to renderer\n   - Bridges extension `postMessage` path from Cocoon with `{handle, message}` shape distinct from workbench-RPC `{panelId, method, params}`\n\n3. Dependency Updates:\n   - Cocoon, Echo, Rest: pozil/auto-assign-issue 2.2.0→3.0.0\n   - Echo: @cloudflare/workers-types, miniflare, wrangler updates\n\n4. Common (c773b79d): Document deprecated aliases UIShowInputBoxRequest and UIShowQuickPickRequest\n\nImpact: Terminal panes, tree views, status bar entries, and command palette entries now render correctly. Extensions can communicate back to Sky UI via the new webview post-message bridge.",
			"SHA": "4c472e3680de51383c1c86ce92ea34c31705db2c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T22:46:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Standardize DTO serialization to camelCase and fix SCM provider registration\n\nSubmodule synchronization across multiple components:\n\n1. Mountain (11b3c822):\n   - Migrate DTO serialization from PascalCase to camelCase across 13 files (CustomDocumentStateDTO, DocumentStateDTO, MarkerDataDTO, etc.) to match the wire format expected by Wind/Sky\n   - Fix SCM provider registration: change PascalCase keys (\"ID\", \"Label\", \"RootUri\") to camelCase (\"id\", \"label\", \"rootUri\") in RegisterScmProvider and add missing \"providerHandle\" field in RegisterScmResourceGroup\n   - Add #[allow(dead_code)] to 15 structs used only in specific build configs\n   - Set MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=10.13 for broader compatibility\n\n2. Mist (94e88d14): Add #![allow(non_snake_case)] lint to permit PascalCase naming conventions consistent with the rest of CodeEditorLand\n\n3. Rest (cf44ea79): Switch binary entry point from Library.rs to Main.rs with proper async tokio runtime\n\nImpact: Wind/Sky now receive correctly formatted DTOs with camelCase keys, SCM source control providers properly register, and the Rest bundler has correct binary structure.",
			"SHA": "3cfc021ed28fb28f64d06171469713f00c88bf0b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T20:30:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add workspace trust handlers for vscode.git and mute vscode-api-gap logs\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing two Mountain changes:\n\n1. Workspace Trust Handlers (bd4aed14):\n   - Implement `Workspace.RequestResourceTrust` and `Workspace.IsResourceTrusted` handlers in Mountain\n   - These route through Mountain instead of falling back to Cocoon's permissive heuristic\n   - vscode.git's `Model.openRepository` calls these before constructing the Repository\n   - Enables `GenerateRouteManifest.sh` to auto-switch Cocoon from heuristic-default to gRPC-routed on next manifest regeneration\n   - Future rounds can replace trust-by-default `true` with real per-OS trust queries (Gatekeeper/SmartScreen/xattrs)\n\n2. Log Noise Reduction:\n   - Mute `vscode-api-gap` dev logs in short mode\n   - These log when extensions use unshimmed vscode API methods - useful for API gap audits but noisy in default dev runs\n   - Enable via `LAND_DEV_LOG=all` or `LAND_DEV_LOG=vscode-api-gap` when needed\n\nImpact: vscode.git extension now properly routes through Mountain's trust handlers with future extensibility for real OS-level trust queries.",
			"SHA": "585327dad2c81eff668676e9412bf4f27fca3b8f"
		},
